{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting","id":1023791,"title":"Undead Menses and shapeshifting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-29T08:58:25-08:00","id":1023791,"title":"Undead Menses and shapeshifting","content":"Let's assume there are at least a few male Acolytes that are eager to tap into the power of Undead Menses for its mystical benefits, but they are unable or unwilling to 'identify as females' and to bargain with their female coven-mates for getting some of their special blood (as a matter of fact, I'm not even sure if it would work for others). They get the mystical reasons about needing to align with the female archetype to tap this boon, but they aren't, and cannot make themselves to be, exactly transgender. At best, perhaps they think the Embrace and the shapeshifting powers it potentially unlocks make sex and gender issues fairly irrelevant for vampires (if you can turn into various kinds of predatory animals, to take a different human form, including the opposite-sex shape, seems no big deal in comparison).<br /> <br /> Would be gender-fluid in the above sense enough to get this Merit ? If not, would buying a power to physically take a female form (not just using Familiar Stranger to cast a female illusion of themselves) and using it enough of a mystical alignment with the feminine to tap this power (by buying the Merit, even if the character is only able to use it in female form) ? I think an argument could be made going this way would be enough of a mystical effort to honor and align with the feminine principle to tap this kind of power, even if the character's gender identity isn't (always or entirely) female, strictly speaking.<br /> <br /> If so, what kind of Devotion or Cruac rite would allow to shapeshift into a different human form, including changing sex ? I assume Protean 3 should be the basis of this Devotion, but I'm unsure if there ought to be other Discipline requirements. I suppose the duration of the change would be indefinite, by analogy with Beast's Skin. As it concerns the blood sorcery method, by looking at the BS guidelines, I suppose a rite to take a different human shape should be Cruac/Transmutation 3 or 4. As a matter of fact, there is a Cruac rite in CotC that allows to take the form (and some memories) of a feeding victim for the night and is rating 4, but it is 1st Edition and perhaps what is needed here does not have to be this powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-29-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:14:57-08:00","id":1023805,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, your game, your rules. But for me, the answer would be emphatically no. The wording of Undead Mensea makes it quite clear that it is <i>gender</i>, not <i>sex</i> that matters for the purposes of qualifying for the Merit. If the character is a woman, she can take the Merit whether she has a penis or a vagina. If the character is a man, or agender, he or they cannot take the Merit, whether he or they have a penis or a vagina. No amount of shapeshifting is going to change your gender, because shapehifting changes your <i>anatomy</i>, and anatomy doesn't matter for the purposes of the Merit.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As for what powers could be used to change a character's sex, in 1st edition the Galloi Bloodline had a unique Devotion that could do it. Although there was a lot of... err... problematic aspects to it involving how well it allowed the character to &quot;pass&quot; as the sex it changed to and what kind of dice rolls you needed to make to pass a medical inspection and shit... I wrote up a 2e update to the Bloodline a while back, which you can find in the homebrew hub if you're interested. For what it's worth, David Hill said he loved it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-29-2016, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:31:32-08:00","id":1023816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023805#post1023805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day, your game, your rules. But for me, the answer would be emphatically no. The wording of Undead Mensea makes it quite clear that it is <i>gender</i>, not <i>sex</i> that matters for the purposes of qualifying for the Merit. If the character is a woman, she can take the Merit whether she has a penis or a vagina. If the character is a man, or agender, he or they cannot take the Merit, whether he or they have a penis or a vagina. No amount of shapeshifting is going to change your gender, because shapehifting changes your <i>anatomy</i>, and anatomy doesn't matter for the purposes of the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, and I'm perfectly aware of the difference between sex and gender, but I'm trying to look beyond the letter of the rule to its spirit, and I would interpret the gender requirement as a mystical need to align with the feminine principle/archetype to tap its power. Since a character cannot change their gender at will (except perhaps by developing and using some kind of specialized self-suggestion mind-control power on themselves), I guessed developing and using a power to change their sex would be enough substitute mystical effort to tap this power. After all, a lot of what vampires are and do is about stealing/cheating/imitating their way into supernatural power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-29-2016, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:38:51-08:00","id":1023822,"title":"","content":"I'd say that changing your sex organ falls under the purview of Protean 2 or 4, without the need for a devotion. Tack on a willpower expenditure requirement to make any morfed changes (semi)permanent. Tack on a time frame requirement. That ought to be enough to show a character's willingness to align their identity with the feminine. Key is that the charcter should be sincere in their identification with the female gender. Perhaps after some time they'll decide to change back or to something else. This should be doable (again through willpower expenditure) and to allow it is well within the limits of any gender-fluidity friendly boundaries.<br /> <br /> (Assuming that you've drained dry at least one woman during your unlife)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 12-29-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T10:12:51-08:00","id":1023839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023822#post1023822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that changing your sex organ falls under the purview of Protean 2 or 4, without the need for a devotion. Tack on a willpower expenditure requirement to make any morfed changes (semi)permanent. Tack on a time frame requirement. That ought to be enough to show a character's willingness to align their identity with the feminine. Key is that the charcter should be sincere in their identification with the female gender. Perhaps after some time they'll decide to change back or to something else. This should be doable (again through willpower expenditure) and to allow it is well within the limits of any gender-fluidity friendly boundaries.<br /> <br /> (Assuming that you've drained dry at least one woman during your unlife)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm dubious if humans qualify as 'predatory or scavenging animal' for the purposes of Protean 2-4. I mean, they do in a scientific sense, but occult systems (within and without the WoD) usually draw a sharp boundary between Man and Beast (Mage Spheres being the only exception I can think of), as indicated by the separation between Animalism and Dominate/Majesty/Nightmare. Having said that, I'm totally in favor of a Protean-only Devotion being able to change one's bodily features, including changing one's sex, on a semi-permanent basis (perhaps rating 2 to make minor changes to facial and bodily features, 3 to make a radical alteration of humanoid form, including a complete sex change, and 4 to add features not usually found in humans). At most, an Obfuscate requirement (with Familiar Stranger) might be necessary to imitate a specific person, or an Auspex requirement (with Lay Open the Mind) to gain their memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T10:21:43-08:00","id":1023841,"title":"","content":"Alright, that's fair. It shouldn't be able to easily out-compete the Familiar Stranger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T10:25:15-08:00","id":1023843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023816#post1023816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, and I'm perfectly aware of the difference between sex and gender, but I'm trying to look beyond the letter of the rule to its spirit, and I would interpret the gender requirement as a mystical need to align with the feminine principle/archetype to tap its power. Since a character cannot change their gender at will (except perhaps by developing and using some kind of specialized self-suggestion mind-control power on themselves), I guessed developing and using a power to change their sex would be enough substitute mystical effort to tap this power. After all, a lot of what vampires are and do is about stealing/cheating/imitating their way into supernatural power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with you on the spirit of the rule. I think the spirit of the rule is granting access to that &quot;archetypal feminine energy&quot; on the basis of actual gender instead of the basis of sex. That should mean that women are able to utilize that feminine power whether they are cis or trans, and men should not be able to utilize it whether they are cis or trans. Changing your anatomy, physiology, etc. won't change the fact that you are a man.<br /> <br /> Now gender is, for many people, a mutable thing, and it's entirely possible that a cis male character who physically changes sex (whether through medical means like Night Doctor Surgery or supernatural means like a Galloi's Transgrssion of Atis or your custom Protean Devotion) to find that their gender also shifts as a result of experiencing unlife in such a body, and then they might be able to qualify for Undead Menses. But if you aren't a woman, you don't get access to that mystical woman power, no matter what body parts you have.<br /> <br /> All that aside, however, let's examine the implications of your interpretation that allows cis male vampires to access Undead Menses if they change their sex. If this is possible, why can trans female vampires who don't transition still access it? Can trans male vampires access it if they don't transition? Do cis female vampires lose access to it if they change their sex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-29-2016, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T10:32:59-08:00","id":1023846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023841#post1023841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, that's fair. It shouldn't be able to easily out-compete the Familiar Stranger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. On one hand, it doesn't allow to imitate specific persons unless you combine Obfuscate in the Devotion. On the other hand, the disguise would be immune to Auspex and other forms of truesight, being a physical change instead of an illusionary glamour. For the sake of completeness, I may also point out that vampires with the Coil of Zirnitra would be able to tap this kind of power by buying Biokinesis and Doppleganger (did I mention how I love this Coil provides a whole new avenue of supernatural power for the mystically-inclined Dragons ?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T11:02:15-08:00","id":1023855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023843#post1023843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with you on the spirit of the rule. I think the spirit of the rule is granting access to that &quot;archetypal feminine energy&quot; on the basis of actual gender instead of the basis of sex. That should mean that women are able to utilize that feminine power whether they are cis or trans, and men should not be able to utilize it whether they are cis or trans. Changing your anatomy, physiology, etc. won't change the fact that you are a man.<br /> <br /> Now gender is, for many people, a mutable thing, and it's entirely possible that a cis male character who physically changes sex (whether through medical means like Night Doctor Surgery or supernatural means like a Galloi's Transgrssion of Atis or your custom Protean Devotion) to find that their gender also shifts as a result of experiencing unlife in such a body, and then they might be able to qualify for Undead Menses. But if you aren't a woman, you don't get access to that mystical woman power, no matter what body parts you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be honest my main problem with this rule is the fact I'm frustrated/uncomfortable with the character background requirement for a strict female gender identity. I'd like to push the boundaries a bit, at least in the sense of making the Merit potentially accessible to genderfluid shapeshifters. Having said that, if we assume a character does change their sex through one of the means we mentioned, becomes a serial shapeshifter, lives part of their unlife as female, and this way makes unlife experiences that let them develop a genderfluid identity over time that includes, cultivates, and appreciates a female part (but does not necessarily reject, neglect, or is uncomfortable with the male part), I'd be satisfied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-29-2016, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T12:07:45-08:00","id":1023879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023855#post1023855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to be honest my main problem with this rule is the fact I'm frustrated/uncomfortable with the character background requirement for a strict female gender identity. I'd like to push the boundaries a bit, at least in the sense of making the Merit potentially accessible to genderfluid shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, now <i>that's</i> a horse of a different color. If your question is how Undead Menses interacts with genders outside the binary, that's something I think there's a lot more room for discussion over (and in fact if I recall correctly, sparking such discussion was the primary reason David chose to base it on gender rather than sex).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023855#post1023855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having said that. if we assume a character does change their sex through one of the means we discussed, becomes a serial shapeshifter, lives part of their unlife as female, and this way makes unlife experiences that let them develop a genderfluid identity over time that includes and appreciates a female part (but does not necessarily reject or neglect the male part), I'd be satisfied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally. There's a lot of room for interpretation here, but personally, I would say characters of nonbinary gender would be able to access Undead Menses in my games, though perhaps not all the time.<br /> <br /> For example, for characters who have a consistent gender that lies somewhere on the spectrum between &quot;strictly male&quot; and &quot;strictly female&quot; (which I believe is the case with basically everyone who's gender doesn't fluctuate), I would allow them to purchase and utilize Undead Menses if their gender leaned more towards the feminine side than the masculine side. And note, that's their gender as they experience it, not their gender expression, sex, or sexual or romantic orientation. For agender characters, I would not allow them to take it. For characters who have multiple genders (such as bigender characters), I would allow them to purchase the Merit and utilize it while in any of their genders that are generally more feminine than masculine (which is something the player would decide). I might even give them a Beat when being in a more masculine gender creates a setback due to not being able to utilize Undead Menses when they needed it. Genderfluid characters would be a bit tougher to rule on, but I would probably handle it pretty much the same way as multi-gender characters; you can buy the Merit, but you can only use it when you are currently leaning feminine, and might grant the player a Beat if you can't use it when you need it due to being in a more masculine-leaning stare. As always, it's up to the player whether their character's gender is over the femininity tipping point or not at any given time.<br /> <br /> In all of the above cases, shapeshifting or any other means of changing sex wouldn't come into consideration at all. Undead Menses doesn't care what your body is like, only what your identity is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T12:22:35-08:00","id":1023887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In all of the above cases, shapeshifting or any other means of changing sex wouldn't come into consideration at all. Undead Menses doesn't care what your body is like, only what your identity is. </div> </div> </div>It might figure into performing the female gender requirement, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T12:26:56-08:00","id":1023889,"title":"","content":"The official rule is not as hard line worded as you're making it out to be. You don't have to have a &quot;strict female gender identity,&quot; you just need to, &quot;identify as female.&quot;<br /> <br /> Even if we're viewing this in terms of modern gender identity, there's the whole spectrum of gender fluid individuals who only need to be in a female headspace to use the Merit, but don't have to identify as female the whole of their existence. You don't need to house rule or change anything to allow gender fluid individuals to access this Merit; it's supposed to be open to them.<br /> <br /> As well, plenty of vampires are much older, and Cruac users are going to be much more likely to hold to spiritual beliefs that incorporate ritual femininity into their practice. Using various ritual practices to become &quot;female&quot; to access feminine linked mystic insight/power fulfills &quot;identify as female,&quot; in a temporary sense just as much as coming at it from a modern perspective of gender does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:04:33-08:00","id":1023904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023879#post1023879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, for characters who have a consistent gender that lies somewhere on the spectrum between &quot;strictly male&quot; and &quot;strictly female&quot; (which I believe is the case with basically everyone who's gender doesn't fluctuate), I would allow them to purchase and utilize Undead Menses if their gender leaned more towards the feminine side than the masculine side. And note, that's their gender as they experience it, not their gender expression, sex, or sexual or romantic orientation. For agender characters, I would not allow them to take it. For characters who have multiple genders (such as bigender characters), I would allow them to purchase the Merit and utilize it while in any of their genders that are generally more feminine than masculine (which is something the player would decide). I might even give them a Beat when being in a more masculine gender creates a setback due to not being able to utilize Undead Menses when they needed it. Genderfluid characters would be a bit tougher to rule on, but I would probably handle it pretty much the same way as multi-gender characters; you can buy the Merit, but you can only use it when you are currently leaning feminine, and might grant the player a Beat if you can't use it when you need it due to being in a more masculine-leaning stare. As always, it's up to the player whether their character's gender is over the femininity tipping point or not at any given time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems a sensible and reasonable approach. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In all of the above cases, shapeshifting or any other means of changing sex wouldn't come into consideration at all. Undead Menses doesn't care what your body is like, only what your identity is. </div> </div> </div>True, but well, it comes into consideration for me. Gender-malleable shapeshifting where sex and identity/orientation changes and experimentation effortlessly and reversibly occur and closely align to each other belongs into my personal sci-fi/fantasy transhumanist utopia and power fantasy, so it is something I can easily identify and sympathize with. Serious disalignment between these axes is something I find much more alien, uncomfortable, and extraneous to my frame of experience (and for that matter serious 'confusion' of genitalia and secondary sex characteristics and the drag aesthetics ring all my squick alarms if I'm forced to contemplate them, no offense intended). For this reason, I rather prefer to deal with this kind of character from the shapeshifting angle. For similar reasons, I also prefer if a character with this Merit only produces menstrual blood from appropriately female organs if genitalia still come into play, the alternative seems... gross.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-29-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:16:34-08:00","id":1023912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023889#post1023889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, plenty of vampires are much older, and Cruac users are going to be much more likely to hold to spiritual beliefs that incorporate ritual femininity into their practice. Using various ritual practices to become &quot;female&quot; to access feminine linked mystic insight/power fulfills &quot;identify as female,&quot; in a temporary sense just as much as coming at it from a modern perspective of gender does.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another sensible way to approach the issue I can easily fit within my own frame of reference and comfort (even if I'd then prefer character w/o female genitalia to be able and produce the 'special' blood the usual, vein-cutting way). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It also seems to fit rather well into the Crone kind of mysticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-29-2016, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:29:06-08:00","id":1023918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023904#post1023904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but well, personally speaking, it comes into consideration for me. Gender-malleable shapeshifting where sex and identity/orientation changes and experimentation closely, effortlessly, and reversibly occur and align to each other belongs into my personal sci-fi/fantasy transhumanist utopia and power fantasy, so it is something I can easily identify and sympathize with.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine, I'm not saying such characters <i>can't</i> utilize shapeshifting to modify their anatomy however they see fit. It's just that if a character, binary or otherwise, has a generally feminine gender, they can utilize Undead Menses regardless of their anatomy. Penis, vagina, both, neither, heck you could even use it in an animal form if you wanted to. That doesn't stop you from only using it while in a human form and with a vagina if that's how you want to do it. But that's not the only way to do it, it's just one option among many.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023904#post1023904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serious disalignment between these two axes or a different kind of change is something I find much more alien, uncomfortable, and extraneous to my frame of experience (and for that matter serious 'confusion' of genitalia and secondary sex characteristics and the drag aesthetics ring my squick alarms, no offense intended).</div> </div> </div> </div>So we're perfectly clear, you have just directly stated to me that my existence (as a genderfluid person who generally identifies as more feminine than masculine but has distinctly &quot;&quot;&quot;male&quot;&quot;&quot; sex characteristics, including a rather full beard at this point in time) squicks you out. Your lack of intent to offend doesn't make it any less transphobic, or any less harmful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023904#post1023904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For this reason, I rather uch prefer to deal with this kind of character from the shapeshifting angle. For similar reasons, I also prefer if a character with this Merit only produces menstrual blood from appropriately female organs if genitalia still come into play, the alternative seems... gross.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking coagulated blood coming out of dead genital oriphices. It's gonna be gross no matter what. Body horror is par for the course in CofD. The fact that you find it more gross when it's a penis that it's coming out of doesn't elicit any sympathy from me, a woman who has a penis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:32:09-08:00","id":1023922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023889#post1023889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The official rule is not as hard line worded as you're making it out to be. You don't have to have a &amp;quot;strict female gender identity,&amp;quot; you just need to, &amp;quot;identify as female.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Even if we're viewing this in terms of modern gender identity, there's the whole spectrum of gender fluid individuals who only need to be in a female headspace to use the Merit, but don't have to identify as female the whole of their existence. You don't need to house rule or change anything to allow gender fluid individuals to access this Merit; it's supposed to be open to them.<br /> <br /> As well, plenty of vampires are much older, and Cruac users are going to be much more likely to hold to spiritual beliefs that incorporate ritual femininity into their practice. Using various ritual practices to become &amp;quot;female&amp;quot; to access feminine linked mystic insight/power fulfills &amp;quot;identify as female,&amp;quot; in a temporary sense just as much as coming at it from a modern perspective of gender does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if this was meant to be in response to me, but I agree with all of it. Sorry if my phrasing made it seem otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:33:53-08:00","id":1023924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023887#post1023887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might figure into performing the female gender requirement, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Seems to me like it would change sex, not gender.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T14:58:11-08:00","id":1023953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023918#post1023918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine, I'm not saying such characters <i>can't</i> utilize shapeshifting to modify their anatomy however they see fit. It's just that if a character, binary or otherwise, has a generally feminine gender, they can utilize Undead Menses regardless of their anatomy. Penis, vagina, both, neither, heck you could even use it in an animal form if you wanted to. That doesn't stop you from only using it while in a human form and with a vagina if that's how you want to do it. But that's not the only way to do it, it's just one option among many.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But it is the option I find most familiar and comfortable for the kind of identification experience RP involves, at least for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So we're perfectly clear, you have just directly stated to me that my existence (as a genderfluid person who generally identifies as more feminine than masculine but has distinctly &quot;&quot;&quot;male&quot;&quot;&quot; sex characteristics, including a rather full beard at this point in time) squicks you out. Your lack of intent to offend doesn't make it any less transphobic, or any less harmful. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I should have been more precise in my statement, but I was trying to avoid being too graphic. The existence and lifestyle of trans people, or interaction with them in any kind of non-extremely sexualized environment, leave me perfectly happy and comfortable. On the other hand, being forced to contemplate graphic or extremely sexualized stuff that overtly and severely violates sexual dimorphism sends me all the wrong instinctual 'Uncanny Valley' signals, and I cannot really control it, not any more than changing what kind of food I find pleasant or what kind of people or sexual experiences I'm attracted to. In other words, please don't force me to look at the wrong kind of erotica, do not drag me to the wrong kind of bedroom, and optimally let me avert my eyes at certain kinds of heavily-sexualized aestethics (if possible). I hope this clarification settles any kind of bad feelings exposition of my experience may have caused, and we can be friends even if we disagree about the kind of stuff we find pleasant in the erotic side of the world. Otherwise, please let's close this tangent by agreeing to respect each other's experiences. I do not want to make anyone feel uncomfortable, nor be made uncomfortable myself. I was just trying to explain why I prefer to use shapeshifting to deal with this kind of character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're talking coagulated blood coming out of dead genital oriphices. It's gonna be gross no matter what. Body horror is par for the course in CofD. The fact that you find it more gross when it's a penis that it's coming out of doesn't elicit any sympathy from me, a woman who has a penis. </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair I am no friend of the 'walking corpse' vision of vampirism to begin with, and extensive reference to 'dead' stuff. I very much prefer to deal with it under the 'mostly, kinda of alive, in the sense other supernatural creatures are, but different in its own way' angle as much as possible. Horror pretty much registers alien and incomprehensible to me, body horror just like mundane disease. I've always dealt with the WoD as a mix of dark fantasy, action-adventure, drama, mystery, and political intrigue, because this is the only way I can find the experience meaningful and worthwhile. And if you ask my personal opinion, menstruation is just another example of how evolution often does things in a suboptimal way, just like vertebrate eyes being wired the wrong way to prevent retinal damage. If I had a choice, nobody should be forced to periodical bleeding from one's genitalia in order to preserve their own fertility. As I said, I rather prefer if any kind of character is able to produce any kind of Vitae the usual, cutting way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-29-2016, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T15:39:31-08:00","id":1023970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023953#post1023953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. But it is the option I find most familiar and comfortable for the kind of identification experience RP involves, at least for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sure. Nothing wrong with that if that's how you want to play your own characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023953#post1023953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I should have been more precise in my statement, but I was trying to avoid being too graphic. The existence and lifestyle of trans people, or interaction with them in any kind of non-extremely sexualized environment, leave me perfectly happy and comfortable. On the other hand, being forced to contemplate graphic or extremely sexualized stuff that severely violates sexual dimorphism sends me all the wrong instinctual 'Uncanny Valley' signals, and I cannot really control it, not any more than changing what kind of food I find pleasant or what kind of people or sexual experiences I'm attracted to. In other words, please don't force me to look at the wrong kind of erotica, do not drag me to the wrong kind of bedroom, and optimally let me avert my eyes at certain kinds of heavily-sexualized aestethics (if possible).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone has any interest in forcing you to do any of those things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023953#post1023953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are certain kind of further nuances about this, but I'm not really sure of how to explain them in a constructive way. I hope this clarification settles any kind of bad feelings exposition of my experience may have caused. Otherwise, please let's close this avenue of discussion by agreeing to respect each other's experiences. I do not want to make anyone feel uncomfortable, nor be made uncomfortable myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, I don't think anything good lies down that line of discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023953#post1023953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to be fair I am no friend of the 'walking corpse' vision of vampirism to begin with, and reference to 'dead' stuff. I very much prefer to deal with it under the 'mostly, kinda of alive, in the sense other supernatural creatures are, but different in its own way' angle as much as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, their biological functions don't... err... function. I certainly wouldn't object to describing their condition as &quot;a kind of life&quot;, as they are objectively animate, conscious, and sentient, and not decomposing. But like, their hearts don't beat, which means their blood doesn't flow, which means its coagulated in their veins and their flesh is pale and cold. No two ways about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023953#post1023953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horror pretty much registers alien and incomprehensible to me, body horror is even worse. I've always dealt with the WoD as a mix of dark fantasy, action-adventure, drama, mystery, and political intrigue, because this is the only way I can find the experience worthwhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023953#post1023953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you ask my personal opinion, menstruation is just another example of how evolution often does things in a suboptimal way, just like vertebrate eyes being wired the wrong way to prevent retinal damage. If I had a choice, nobody should be forced to periodical bleeding from one's genitalia in order to preserve their own fertility. As I said, I rather prefer if any kind of character is able to produce any kind of Vitae the usual, cutting way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your game, your rules, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T16:09:11-08:00","id":1023984,"title":"","content":"*pokes head in*<br /> <br /> *finds Irioth being himself*<br /> <br /> *leaves*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T16:22:29-08:00","id":1023988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023970#post1023970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, their biological functions don't... err... function. I certainly wouldn't object to describing their condition as &quot;a kind of life&quot;, as they are objectively animate, conscious, and sentient, and not decomposing. But like, their hearts don't beat, which means their blood doesn't flow, which means its coagulated in their veins and their flesh is pale and cold. No two ways about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the sake of plausibility and consistency, not to mention minimizing the gross 'zombie' quotient, I rather prefer to assume vampire blood never, ever coagulates and remains entirely fluid as long as it is within their body, even if it doesn't flow if the blush of life is not active. I mean, it is fairly easy to prevent coagulation of static blood even for mundane science and technology, or blood banks wouldn't exist. Surely the Requiem can do much better. Just assume the Kindred naturally have some kind of really, really good anticoagulant, and use their efficient voluntary control of their own body tissues and fluids (short of being able to violate magical conservation of energy) to deal with potential blood loss. Coagulation seems a needless, pointless complication for them. If would mean they'd have to re-fluidify their blood every time they use the blush of life, or spill Vitae for all kinds of uses. It would be much more complex and odd than suppressing coagulation in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-29-2016, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T16:46:28-08:00","id":1023998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023924#post1023924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? Seems to me like it would change sex, not gender.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a changed sex may assist a person to successfully perform their gender identity. See: post-op ambitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T17:02:14-08:00","id":1024004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023904#post1023904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but well, it comes into consideration for me. Gender-malleable shapeshifting where sex and identity/orientation changes and experimentation effortlessly and reversibly occur and closely align to each other belongs into my personal sci-fi/fantasy transhumanist utopia and power fantasy, so it is something I can easily identify and sympathize with. Serious disalignment between these axes is something I find much more alien, uncomfortable, and extraneous to my frame of experience (and for that matter serious 'confusion' of genitalia and secondary sex characteristics and the drag aesthetics ring all my squick alarms if I'm forced to contemplate them, no offense intended). For this reason, I rather prefer to deal with this kind of character from the shapeshifting angle. For similar reasons, I also prefer if a character with this Merit only produces menstrual blood from appropriately female organs if genitalia still come into play, the alternative seems... gross.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of response sounds rather appropriate for the Circle of the Crone to me, regardless of what causes it. Now &quot;sci-fi/fantasy transhumanist utopia and power fantasy&quot; on the other hand, is far more Ordo Dracul.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T17:20:48-08:00","id":1024011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024004#post1024004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sort of response sounds rather appropriate for the Circle of the Crone to me, regardless of what causes it. Now &quot;sci-fi/fantasy transhumanist utopia and power fantasy&quot; on the other hand, is far more Ordo Dracul.</div> </div> </div> </div>How appropriate. Guess which two Covenants I self-identify with ?<br /> <br /> By the way, we discussed two approaches I find most useful to the issue: using occult props and self-suggestion to temporarily put oneself in the 'right' female identity mystical frame of mind for ritual purposes, and using shapeshifting powers and subsequent unlife experiences to gradually change one's gender identity, quite possibly in a serial way. No doubt, both paths would involve a good deal of RP for the on-screen scenes, and player's description for the off-screen scenes. However, the former approach might well warrant some kind of roll to check how effectively the character persuades the self and whatever forces power Cruac they are currently feminine-aligned. What might be appropriate ? I am guessing a Meditation roll, but Empathy or Occult might just as well enter the picture, or even Expression or Subterfuge.<br /> <br /> As it concerns the latter approach, how much time and effort (I suppose, the more the vampire interacts with other people the 'right' way, especially mortals, the quicker and better) would it typically take for the identity change to take place ? The process involved here seems kind of reverse of the usual RL one, where (for what I know) people usually start with a certain identity and change their body and environment to adapt them to it. Here someone would use body and environment changes to induce an identity change. From my own perspective, I'd guess months if it is being done the first time, or weeks, if the character is already experiences with this kind of change, depending on the amount of social activity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-29-2016, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T17:59:46-08:00","id":1024029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024011#post1024011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, we discussed two approaches I find most useful to the issue: using occult props and self-suggestion to temporarily put oneself in the 'right' female identity mystical frame of mind for ritual purposes, and using shapeshifting powers and subsequent unlife experiences to gradually change one's gender identity, quite possibly in a serial way. No doubt, both paths would involve a good deal of RP for the on-screen scenes, and player's description for the off-screen scenes. However, the former approach might well warrant some kind of roll to check how effectively the character persuades the self and whatever forces power Cruac they are currently feminine-aligned, barring an exceptional RP performance. What might be appropriate ? I am guessing a Meditation roll, but Empathy and Occult might just as well enter the picture, or even Expression and Subterfuge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeeuuughhh, judging whether or not a player's RP performance is &quot;feminine enough&quot; to warrant use of the Merit without a roll sounds <i>really</i> iffy to me. I'd say if you're going to make it require a roll, it should just require a roll. If you're going to just let it work, it should just work. If you want to make it require a roll, Meditation seems fairly appropriate. I could see Resolve + Empathy as well, but probably not Occult and definitely not Manipulation, Expression, or Subterfuge due to unfortunate implications.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024011#post1024011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it concerns the latter approach, how much time and effort (I suppose, the more the vampire interacts with other people the 'right' way, especially mortals, the quicker and better) would it typically take for the identity change to take place ? The process involved here seems kind of reverse of the usual RL one, where (for what I know) people usually start with a certain identity and change their body and environment to adapt them to it. Here someone would use body and environment changes to induce an identity change. From my own optimistic, can-do perspective, I'd guess months if it is being done the first time, or weeks, if the character is already experiences with this kind of change, depending on the amount of social activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not necessarily the reverse of how it works in real life. I know a few other trans people who came to terms with their identities only after experimenting with their gender expression, or after being mistakenly referred to by feminine honorifics online and realizing it felt &quot;right&quot; to them to be referred to that way. People come to their identities through all sorts of avenues. As for how long it might take, it's different for every individual. It might take months or even years of grappling with your own thoughts and emotions before finding what fits, or it might just click the first time you slip into a more feminine role that this suits you better. It should definitely be something the player and the storyteller work closely together on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T19:18:13-08:00","id":1024059,"title":"","content":"As someone with a <i>very</i> weak gender identity*, this discussion baffles me a bit - why aren't you just using a Dominate devotion to selectively edit your gender so you can get some of that sweet, sweet menstruating corpse action?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* Agender, I think the term is? Gender straight-up doesn't factor into my self-identity, and it annoys me when other people assume it does.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T19:21:48-08:00","id":1024063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024029#post1024029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eeeeeuuughhh, judging whether or not a player's RP performance is &quot;feminine enough&quot; to warrant use of the Merit without a roll sounds <i>really</i> iffy to me. I'd say if you're going to make it require a roll, it should just require a roll. If you're going to just let it work, it should just work. If you want to make it require a roll, Meditation seems fairly appropriate. I could see Resolve + Empathy as well, but probably not Occult and definitely not Manipulation, Expression, or Subterfuge due to unfortunate implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point about the RP issue - on second thoughts, I changed my own mind and edited the point myself, since I see the problem. I thought of Occult, Expression, or Subterfuge just because we were talking about using the Merit right in the context of a Crone ritual, which you know, is a kind of performance. I agree Resolve, Composure, and/or Empathy, if any, would be much more appropriate outside of that (after all, the Merit is useful even for Disciplines). I honestly cannot make up my mind ATM whether it's better with a roll or w/o it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not necessarily the reverse of how it works in real life. I know a few other trans people who came to terms with their identities only after experimenting with their gender expression, or after being mistakenly referred to by feminine honorifics online and realizing it felt &quot;right&quot; to them to be referred to that way. People come to their identities through all sorts of avenues. As for how long it might take, it's different for every individual. It might take months or even years of grappling with your own thoughts and emotions before finding what fits, or it might just click the first time you slip into a more feminine role that this suits you better. It should definitely be something the player and the storyteller work closely together on. </div> </div> </div>True, and I guess this reference would fit those Acolytes just right who happen to be pre-Embrace potential trans, and I guess the Circle or the Ordo would attract a fair deal of them. I wonder how different it would be for those characters who instead decide to engage in this kind of change, however sincere, for power's sake, without any special kind of potential. Do we have examples of people who engaged in serious TG mostly for practical reasons ? I would guess some examples might exist in entertainment, but it is a chicken-and-egg question. And our RL experience in this field is woefully constrained by the limits of technology. We lack reference from a society where all kinds of self-expression and experimention, gendered or not, in body and mind, are just as simple, reversible, and available as changing one's clothes or hair. That would better approximate what certain WoD supernaturals may experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T19:39:38-08:00","id":1024067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024059#post1024059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone with a <i>very</i> weak gender identity*, this discussion baffles me a bit - why aren't you just using a Dominate devotion to selectively edit your gender so you can get some of that sweet, sweet menstruating corpse action?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose this might indeed be a worthwhile option as well. I think someone raised it at some point, but the discussion didn't catch up on it. Well, let's see. I'd assume this kind of psychic change is prima facie the rough equivalent of Conditioning or The Lying Mind, only done on yourself, and you are not really resisting, so it can be done rather more quickly. So Dominate 4. But if the subject already has some substantial internalized experience about the way the other gender thinks and acts, and/or already went through this kind of change, a more superficial alteration may suffice, equivalent to the Iron Edict. Or for my own preferences' and completeness' sake, optimally combine Dominate 2/4 and Protean 3 in one Devotion, to change yourself, body and mind, in one fell sweep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-29-2016, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T20:24:41-08:00","id":1024081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024059#post1024059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone with a <i>very</i> weak gender identity*, this discussion baffles me a bit - why aren't you just using a Dominate devotion to selectively edit your gender so you can get some of that sweet, sweet menstruating corpse action?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's this kind of thing that keeps me coming back to these forums. Dead people mind-controlling themselves into being women so they can perform menstruation magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T01:43:24-08:00","id":1024154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024081#post1024081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's this kind of thing that keeps me coming back to these forums. Dead people mind-controlling themselves into being women so they can perform menstruation magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, the sobering, grounding benefits of the outside perspective. And yet, I bet this is far from the three most bizarre things being discussed on a forum like this one any given week. It has been an interesting ride, and apologies to anyone getting hit from my online foot-in-mouth disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-30-2016, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:38:48-08:00","id":1024222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024081#post1024081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dead people mind-controlling themselves into being women so they can perform menstruation magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I miss the forums for, like, two days, and I find precious lines like this. This is why I can't take my eyes off this place.<br /> <br /> ... And now I suspect I've been ghouled by someone who's been using the internet to channel Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T05:00:46-08:00","id":1024233,"title":"","content":"So I mean. The group of people who are likely to raise hell about the cis male taking undead manses (as oppossed to not caring or mocking) are also the group of people who tend to proport that other people can't force labels on you.<br /> <br /> So take undead menses for your cis male character, just weather the heckling, and if anyone raises hell demand they explain to you in clear terms what would be &quot;woman enough&quot; to take it.<br /> <br /> I'm not aaying this is anything but a jerk response, I'm proporting that it would be an effective one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:11:09-08:00","id":1024338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024233#post1024233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I mean. The group of people who are likely to raise hell about the cis male taking undead manses (as oppossed to not caring or mocking) are also the group of people who tend to proport that other people can't force labels on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>And which people are those, exactly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024233#post1024233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So take undead menses for your cis male character, just weather the heckling, and if anyone raises hell demand they explain to you in clear terms what would be &quot;woman enough&quot; to take it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says right there in the Merit. You have to identify as female. If the character identifies as male, cis or otherwise, he doesn't qualify for the Merit. If the character identifies as female, she doesn't have to <i>do</i> anything to be &quot;woman enough&quot;, but at that point the character isn't a cis male.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024233#post1024233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not aaying this is anything but a jerk response, I'm proporting that it would be an effective one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, as it conflates gender identity with gender expression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-30-2016, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T09:04:17-08:00","id":1024366,"title":"","content":"I know the text in the quote was not directed to me but I'd like to answer the first question:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024338#post1024338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And which people are those, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>The assertion defined as to who the group is<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I mean. <u>The group of people who are likely to raise hell about the cis male taking undead manses</u> (as oppossed to not caring or mocking) are also<u> the group of people who tend to proport that other people can't force labels on you.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>The group of people who &quot;tend to purport that other people can't force labels on you&quot; is a large swath of people. I am not among those people as I recognize labels as both useful for identity and perceptual shortcuts. I do like strict definition and like clear language which this merit is written in. Given I am not part of that group I can't added my anecdotal account. I would say based on evidence that people actually can force labels on other through basic observation of reality, that large swath of people are incorrect in the matter that defines them as a group in this case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024338#post1024338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says right there in the Merit. You have to identify as female. If the character identifies as male, cis or otherwise, he doesn't qualify for the Merit. If the character identifies as female, she doesn't have to <i>do</i> anything to be &quot;woman enough&quot;, but at that point the character isn't a cis male.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I read the merit as well and by definition of the terms involved is correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024338#post1024338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, as it conflates gender identity with gender expression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Valid point, it does combine those two concepts when they are not necessarily one, though one tends to lead to the other as identity does tend (though not always) lead to expression of identity.<br /> <br /> To comment on the conversion:<br /> <br /> If this was an exchange of images instead of words, it'd a series of Venn diagrams and it might benefit from the clarity granted by that form of communication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-30-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T09:54:24-08:00","id":1024379,"title":"","content":"Hrm... perhaps my phrasing is bad. What I mean is, you can act / talk / look / etc. Like a cis male and continue to play the character you want to play, totally ignoring everything about idebtifyibg as a woman except the identifying part. Your RP doesn't have to actually change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T10:32:03-08:00","id":1024392,"title":"","content":"Hence why I suggest Dominate - it's not like brain-hacking yourself has <i>any</i> negative consequences that would make for some fun plot developments.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yay ladyparts thank you Protean&quot; doesn't have the same <i>punch</i> to it, really.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024379#post1024379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your RP doesn't have to actually change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boo! Your RP should be <i>continuously</i> changing in small and exciting ways - otherwise, you're just playing a caricature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 12-30-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T12:18:30-08:00","id":1024444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024379#post1024379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm... perhaps my phrasing is bad. What I mean is, you can act / talk / look / etc. Like a cis male and continue to play the character you want to play, totally ignoring everything about idebtifyibg as a woman except the identifying part. Your RP doesn't have to actually change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoken like someone who has never experienced living as a female-identifying person while presenting in a typically-masculine manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T07:05:56-08:00","id":1024746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1024444#post1024444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoken like someone who has never experienced living as a female-identifying person while presenting in a typically-masculine manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoken like someone who is presenting a path thve have aknowledged and highlighted as being overly dismissive and frowned upon... but still a path. That said, not every character needs to present or emphasize every aspect of who they are at all times. Further, if we are going to think in terms of sociological impact (which I dont think is a good idea, unless someone is sitting down at their game to do that) then I could think of few things more pro unity/acceptance/tolotance then a male taking this merit, aknowledging they fulfill the requirements, and then sitting on that plot thread for the rest of the game--though I would step in if it became an uncomfortable mockery. <br /> <br /> Generally speaking, I would predict that people who would do this woulf fall in at least one of three camps...<br /> A. People who only care aboit the mechanics. In this case branding trans as a positive mechanical effect in their case is the most useful thing you could hope for.<br /> B. They are ignorant of the trans experience. In this case. In this case, unless they are unusually receptive to instruction through play, normalizing the experience is hands down the best way to change the minds at the table. Were I an ST, I might try to give juuuuuuust enough tension that they were in the habit of forcing others to accept their decision to be normal, equal, and not something to persecute. That habit will likey, subconciously transfer to their behavior outside of the game.<br /> C. They are well aware of the trans experience and as such they should really be allowed to present or ignore that however they damn well please.<br /> <br /> Personally, again, not the criteria I would use... but hey. That's the pro unity logic.<br /> <br /> Also, it's probably better to not make assumptions about someone's life or assume that everyone has the same (or even similar) experiences / response / etc. things as you. It almost always does more harm than good, and there are kinder and more constructive ways to present your dissent.<br /> <br /> Saying that my argument is &quot;speaking like someone [who isn't part of group X]&quot; gives the impression that disagreeing with me (and by extension implicitly agreeing with you) is a <i>necessary</i> part of being X. There are two issues with this. <br /> <br /> First, it is basically the argument that you are correct because of consensus and solidarity. I can go on for ages why that is a terrifying thing in the best of times, but right now Ill emphasize how it shuts down discussion. It can be summed up as &quot;come at me bro, also my peeps are behind me&quot; (they may or may not be behind you) which also gives a hostile tone to the conversation. You have no arguments to really respond to, except the assertion that for some reason I can't speak on a subject because I'm a terrible person, or otherwise disqualified from being able to voice a valid opinion. Silencing someone or spreading the idea that their voice has no value is... well lets say it invites an unpleasant response.<br /> <br /> Second, and most importantly, it is exclusionary to a degree I don't think you are going for. One time won't make a difference, but over time that sort of thing being a habit pushes all groups into the more extreme spectrum of their thinking by victimizing their own people. This because you are also implicitly saying that anyone *else* who disagrees with you or agrees with me isn't a part of your group. While this galvenizes the core people who do disagree with you, it pushes others away and makes them less likely to seek fellowship / assistance. If they have a strong sense of identity wrapped up in being a female identifying person presenting as typically male but they also don't have a strong relevant support network this can, over time, be catestrophic. I do emphasize repeated instances over time, such that it becomes part of the percieved culture.<br /> <br /> So, in short, I am speaking like SoulGambit, a person you do not know with life experiences you are unfamiliar with. While you may have felt justified in presenting your dissent in that manner I respectfully request that you find alternative methods in the future because it has a negative impact on the discussion, on the culture of the forums, and on the broader community we both love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T10:45:55-08:00","id":1024824,"title":"","content":"@SoulGambit...<br /> <br /> <i>You just menstruated out of your male corpse's penis</i>. What's more, you're in a culture that is <i>very</i> aware that this is something that only happens to vampires that identify as female. You <i>really</i> don't think that your vamp is going to be doing some soul-searching?<br /> <br /> And <i>don't</i> give me the whole &quot;He totally identifies as female, except he doesn't display it in any way!&quot; garbage - that's called &quot;I want the cool menstruation super-power, but I don't want it to actually change my character&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T21:23:02-08:00","id":1025286,"title":"","content":"Wow my last post was done on telephone and it shows... sorry for the spelling / grammar.<br /> <br /> If you whip out your undead penis in public well... ..m thats really on you, isn't it? Also not only is there nothing in the merit to suggest how that happens, its pretty symbolically inappropriate.<br /> <br /> But yes, &quot;i want cool menstration super-powers&quot; is not only hands down the weirdest sentance to ever come out of my love for V:tM, but it is probably the reason they invest in the merit that gives them cool menstration powers.<br /> <br /> For what its worth I wouldn't even put it on my female characters, much less male or neutral gendered. I can't think of a way to ever present that mechanic in a way that I feel comfortable with in public, or in a way that doesn't make the character less cool for having it. I'm sure thats my own failing, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T22:13:33-08:00","id":1025296,"title":"","content":"You wouldn't need to whip out your dick, I wouldn't think.<br /> <br /> I think having magic that involves <i>excreting blood</i> in a society full of people who have super-human senses <i>specifically honed</i> towards detecting blood is something that you <i>really</i> wouldn't be able to keep a lid on for long. At the very least, you'd have some Mekhet making snide and/or supportive comments - hey, some of those fashion tips might come in handy, you know.<br /> <br /> Also, where <i>else</i> would it come from? It's the closest corresponding part your meat-shell has, so...<br /> <br /> As for my &quot;you just want cool menstruation super-powers&quot; comment, the point I was trying (and failing) to get across is that the impression that I was getting was &quot;I want cool menstruation super-powers, <i>but I don't want any of the other stuff that entails</i>&quot;. Also, it's not even a cool menstruation super-power - it's more like a kind-of-acceptable-but-already-too-utterly-ridiculous-when-it-showed-up-in-V:tM menstruation super-power.<br /> <br /> I kinda laughed when I first saw it, mostly in disbelief that they had wasted wordcount on it. But then <i>dumb amounts of wordcount</i> was wasted on the Idigam in W:tF 2e, so I ended up seeing a pattern and shrugging.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Concerning weird sentences, I once tried to explain to a friend why &quot;self-aware virus that turns those who it infects into a copy of the original 15-your-old girl who served as Patient Zero&quot; is a <i>perfectly valid</i> concept for a super-hero.<br /> <br /> Given that I got &quot;someone so super-humanly fashionable it wrecks the time-space continuum&quot; accepted for a game, I think I'll keep trying with Infectious Girl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T22:38:28-08:00","id":1025310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1023953#post1023953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) if you ask my personal opinion, menstruation is just another example of how evolution often does things in a suboptimal way, just like vertebrate eyes being wired the wrong way to prevent retinal damage. If I had a choice, nobody should be forced to periodical bleeding from one's genitalia in order to preserve their own fertility. As I said, I rather prefer if any kind of character is able to produce any kind of Vitae the usual, cutting way.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1025286#post1025286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what its worth I wouldn't even put it on my female characters, much less male or neutral gendered. I can't think of a way to ever present that mechanic in a way that I feel comfortable with in public, or in a way that doesn't make the character less cool for having it. I'm sure thats my own failing, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to point out the irony in the fact that the folks who are arguing in favor of male characters being able to take Undead Menses <i>d</i><i>on't actually want a menstruation power</i>.<br /> <br /> Guys.<br /> <br /> If you want a power that lets you produce blood that grants 8-again on cruac rolls but don't want to have to play as girl or think about icky biological functions women have to deal with, just re-name the Merit &quot;Ritual Bleeder&quot; or something and remove the &quot;must identify as female&quot; requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T20:29:43-08:00","id":1026294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1025310#post1025310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I just want to point out the irony in the fact that the folks who are arguing in favor of male characters being able to take Undead Menses <i>d</i><i>on't actually want a menstruation power</i>.<br /> <br /> Guys.<br /> <br /> If you want a power that lets you produce blood that grants 8-again on cruac rolls but don't want to have to play as girl or think about icky biological functions women have to deal with, just re-name the Merit &quot;Ritual Bleeder&quot; or something and remove the &quot;must identify as female&quot; requirement.</div> </div> </div> </div>If intent matters, Charlaquin's commentary throughout this thread has been spot-on with my thoughts on that Merit's application.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:31:22-08:00","id":1026956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1025310#post1025310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I just want to point out the irony in the fact that the folks who are arguing in favor of male characters being able to take Undead Menses <i>d</i><i>on't actually want a menstruation power</i>.<br /> <br /> Guys.<br /> <br /> If you want a power that lets you produce blood that grants 8-again on cruac rolls but don't want to have to play as girl or think about icky biological functions women have to deal with, just re-name the Merit &quot;Ritual Bleeder&quot; or something and remove the &quot;must identify as female&quot; requirement.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I see ample thematic ground, in the occult source material Undead Menses channels to represent the mystical power of the feminine archetype and its fertility, to justify the existence of a similar Merit, reserved to male characters (see below about what this entails), that represents the mystical power of the masculine archetype and its fertility. In this context, the closest, most natural masculine equivalent of menstrual blood for the feminine would be sperm. So following this reasoning it seems the male fertility Merit would be available to characters that identify as a male AND are able to produce sperm after activating the blush of life.<br /> <br /> Yes, this would seem to place an additional anatomical hurdle to clear for trans characters to use this merit, but this comes from the fact the universe originally made the mystically relevant female fertility substance blood, while it is sperm for males. This would be where the sex-change applications of Protean or Night Doctor Surgery we previously discussed would come useful. Frankly I find the notion of replacing sperm, or menstrual blood for that matter, with blood supposed to come out from a penis gross enough that I'm not willing to contemplate it for long or bring it at my table if I can avoid it, regardless of the additional hurdles this might impose on certain characters. Then again, if we are willing to allow the 'special fertility substance' to be replaced by Vitae that can be spilled the usual vein-cutting way, I'd be much more willing to allow (and require) the substitution. However, I'm not entirely persuaded it would be mystically appropriate, but then again, it might be fitting for vampires.<br /> <br /> At the moment the creatively challenged me cannot think of a better name for the male version of the Merit than 'Undead Sperm'. I suppose there might well be a good name for the unified version of the Merit that covers both options, even if I cannot think of it atm. 'Ritual Bleeder' might or might not be entirely appropriate depending on the issue I mentioned before. On second thoughts, I might be willing to require blush of life to be active to use any version of this Merit for anyone, female or male, because of its mystical ties with fertility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-05-2017, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T06:30:15-08:00","id":1026993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1026956#post1026956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I see ample thematic ground, in the occult source material Undead Menses channels to represent the mystical power of the feminine archetype and its fertility, to justify the existence of a similar Merit, reserved to male characters (see below about what this entails), that represents the mystical power of the masculine archetype and its fertility. In this context, the closest, most natural masculine equivalent of menstrual blood for the feminine would be sperm. So following this reasoning it seems the male fertility Merit would be available to characters that identify as a male AND are able to produce sperm after activating the blush of life.<br /> <br /> Yes, this would seem to place an additional anatomical hurdle to clear for trans characters to use this merit, but this comes from the fact the universe originally made the mystically relevant female fertility substance blood, while it is sperm for males. This would be where the sex-change applications of Protean or Night Doctor Surgery we previously discussed would come useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>That logic is inconsistent with the way Undead Menses works. Trans women can't produce menstrual blood, but the Merit is still available to them. I see no reason an equivalent Merit for men wouldn't work the same way. In fact, it's much easier for trans men to produce come than for trans women to produce blood from their penises. Granted, the come wouldn't contain sperm, but nor is the blood produced by a trans woman with Undead Menses actually menstrual. It's the symbolism that matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1026956#post1026956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I find the notion of replacing sperm, or menstrual blood for that matter, with blood supposed to come out from a penis gross enough that I'm not willing to contemplate it for long or bring it at my table if I can avoid it, regardless of the additional hurdles this might impose on certain characters. Then again, if we are willing to allow the 'special fertility substance' to be replaced by Vitae that can be spilled the usual vein-cutting way, I'd be much more willing to allow (and require) the substitution. However, I'm not entirely persuaded it would be mystically appropriate, but then again, it might be fitting for vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your discomfort with ordinary bodily functions that involve genitals is duly noted. Once again, if you want a power for producing special ritual blood but don't want it to come out of the user's genitals and want it to be available to characters of any gender, it seems like the best solution for you would just be to take Undead Menses, change the name, remove the gender requirement, and say it's produced &quot;in the usual, vein-cutting way.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1026956#post1026956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment the creatively challenged me cannot think of a better name for the male version of the Merit than 'Undead Sperm'.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Undead Seed&quot; seems like the obvious choice here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1026956#post1026956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose there might well be a good name for the unified version of the Merit that covers both options, even if I cannot think of it atm. 'Ritual Bleeder' might or might not be entirely appropriate depending on the issue I mentioned before. On second thoughts, I might be willing to require blush of life to be active to use any version of this Merit for anyone, female or male, because of its mystical ties with fertility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ritual Bleeder was proposed as a name for a hypothetical equivalent, gender-neutral Merit that produces the blood &quot;in the usual, vein-cutting way&quot; so that you can preserve your sensibilities regarding genital fluids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:04:16-08:00","id":1027034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1026993#post1026993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Undead Seed&quot; seems like the obvious choice here.</div> </div> </div> </div>And is well suited to stand in the fertility/virility cult based theme. In my thinking it may be better to change the prerequisite from simple gender identity which has no mechanics to membership (even one dot) in a Mystery Cult Initiation that has the types of beliefs implied by the merit which also fits the role the Vampire would play. I mean if I was going to Homebrew it to tap into occult belief and practices based on Gender Roles and/or Identity (though arguable use of the merit would be use of the Role, I mean it is an occult ritual where you are playing a part thus a Role). Plenty of historic cults of virility and fertility both so, while one cult may elevate femaleness, maleness, or both and thus that cult only have access to the portion they have in their doctrine, both versions are equally valid in the Chronicles of Darkness. (Renaming and re-flavoring merits is even listed in the book, and this seems like an obvious example where this can be applied). Plus I like encouraging Mystery Cult Initiation because it makes a part of the setting the players are invested in that is pretty flavorful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1026993#post1026993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ritual Bleeder was proposed as a name for a hypothetical equivalent, gender-neutral Merit that produces the blood &quot;in the usual, vein-cutting way&quot; so that you can preserve your sensibilities regarding genital fluids.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true, but adding context adds flavor to the merit, though it need not be the gender based context listed in this thread or in the book to be interesting. I would keep it occult/cult flavored, due to this being the Circle of Crone, perhaps tie it to another trope often with associated fringe/archaic religious practices. Thoughts that comes to mind are ritual sacrifices (possibly in the form of deadly ceremonial feeding), or working in certain configuration of cabals and covens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-05-2017, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T11:50:52-08:00","id":1027187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1026993#post1026993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your discomfort with ordinary bodily functions that involve genitals is duly noted.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's really no reason to be condescending here. This is a perfectly normal hangup (there's a reason &quot;Tolerance for Biology&quot; is a merit rather than default) and &quot;blood from a penis&quot; is not &quot;ordinary bodily functions&quot; besides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T12:35:36-08:00","id":1027221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1027187#post1027187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's really no reason to be condescending here. This is a perfectly normal hangup (there's a reason &amp;quot;Tolerance for Biology&amp;quot; is a merit rather than default) and &amp;quot;blood from a penis&amp;quot; is not &amp;quot;ordinary bodily functions&amp;quot; besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, I apologize for my bad attitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:50:39-08:00","id":1027650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1027187#post1027187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's really no reason to be condescending here. This is a perfectly normal hangup (there's a reason &quot;Tolerance for Biology&quot; is a merit rather than default) and &quot;blood from a penis&quot; is not &quot;ordinary bodily functions&quot; besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I am not really squeamish about biological fluids (it would be a significant problem with working in my chosen field, if not an immediate one given my specialization) but copious blood coming out from a penis is almost always a sign of serious trauma or disease, much more so than cutting a finger or a wrist, which can easily be a trivial wound if done the right way or having the kind of healing factor vampires have. My medical training keeps screaming in my head that a bleeding penis is not 'ordinary bodily functions' when I face the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-06-2017, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:51:32-08:00","id":1027652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1027221#post1027221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fair, I apologize for my bad attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense was taken. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:47:26-08:00","id":1027699,"title":"","content":"To be clear, I was referring to ordinary mensturation when I said &quot;normal bodily functions.&quot; Undead Menses is not ordinary menstruation, it's just symbolic of menstruation. That's why it doesn't matter if the ritualist using it has anatomy that is naturally capable of menstruation or not, only if they are metaphysically aligned with the symbolism of the menstrual cycle and feminine creative power. If the reality of blood coming out of genital orifices that it isn't supposed to come out of makes you uncomfortable (understandably so - it <i>is</i> meant as body horror), there's nothing wrong with altering the narrative a bit to say that the special ritual blood produced by the Merit is bled from the wrist instead of the genitals. That <i>would</i> negatively impact the symbolic association with menstruation, but that may or may not be a problem for you. Particularly if you want characters who's gender incorporates a generous portion of masculinity to be able to use the Merit as well, it seems like divorcing the &quot;I produce special ritual blood&quot; Merit from menstrual symbolism and making it accessible to everyone kind of kills two birds with one stone for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T22:13:12-08:00","id":1028430,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, it would actually be mythically resonant for trans-women with Undead Menses to castrate themselves as part of the action necessary to draw out the blood.<br /> <br /> Take 1L from lopping off an unnecessary body part, regrow it by tomorrow evening. Simples!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T03:51:47-08:00","id":1028487,"title":"","content":"I've never really looked over the merit (I typically play male characters), but I figured it lent more towards a feminine slant because from what I gather the Circle of the Crone was presented as more of a feminine thing in second edition; this slant was reinforced by the Circle being called the Mother's Army, the Mother-Daughter Bond merit, and of course the Undead Menses merit.<br /> <br /> Likewise I've always looked at the Lancea et Sanctum with a more masculine slant; this slant was reinforced by the mentions of Monks and how the Lancea et Sanctum typically reminds me of the Catholic Church in second edition.<br /> <br /> I also look at it from a more societal aspect; pagan cults would be more focused on femininity because the Church at large would focus more on masculinity. I imagined that the Circle of the Crone and the Lancea et Sanctum would hold similar practices. This is seen in the sorceries of the covenants; Cruac evokes a primal feel (women were often attributed to being more emotionally invested) with how blood is sacrficed upon an altar, and Theban Sorcery evokes a much more judgmental feeling (men were often attributed to being better leaders and judges of character) with how the Dark Miracles are performed.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm fine with Undead Menses being just for women, but I can understand that some people would prefer something that would celebrate their masculinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T17:53:31-08:00","id":1029379,"title":"","content":"I have to say, this thread is <i>hysterical</i> when run through the gender-swapping bookmarklet I picked up a while ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:00:29-08:00","id":1031752,"title":"","content":"Ok so with our 20/20 hind sight I'm inclined to believe that the merit in question may have been better named something like &quot;ritual blood offering&quot; and made usable with any blood sorcerery (bleeding from the wounds of Christ giving bonuses to Theban Sorcery is very in theme).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:12:45-08:00","id":1031762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1031752#post1031752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so with our 20/20 hind sight I'm inclined to believe that the merit in question may have been better named something like &quot;ritual blood offering&quot; and made usable with any blood sorcerery (bleeding from the wounds of Christ giving bonuses to Theban Sorcery is very in theme).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Stigmata is a vastly different thing that has its own Merit. Biblically, the menstrual cycle is seen as unclean to extreme degrees. You need monthly animal sacrifice just to cleanse yourself of your sin, but everything you've touched in that period is unclean, any man who has seen it is also unclean and in that circumstance, 'both shall be cut off from other people.'<br /> <br /> Cruac views it as an empowering and natural thing.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't make sense for menstrual blood to be used for Lancea et Sanctum rituals unless the ritualist was a blasphemer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:31:12-08:00","id":1031777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1031752#post1031752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so with our 20/20 hind sight I'm inclined to believe that the merit in question may have been better named something like &amp;quot;ritual blood offering&amp;quot; and made usable with any blood sorcerery (bleeding from the wounds of Christ giving bonuses to Theban Sorcery is very in theme).</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. The Merit as-written encourages body-positivivity, giving a positive connotation to an undeservedly stigmatized aspect of human biology. It encourages trans representation by giving transfeminine characters access to a Merit on the basis of being feminine. It generates discussion of gender. And it does all of it in a way that is highly thematically appropriate for the Circle of the Crone. There's certainly nothing wrong with generalizing the Merit in your home game, and I encourage folks to do so if they want a similar power to be accessible to male characters or to disassociate the power from mensturation. But as a default I think its specificity is to its great advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T23:12:33-08:00","id":1032504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1023791-undead-menses-and-shapeshifting?p=1031777#post1031777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. The Merit as-written encourages body-positivivity, giving a positive connotation to an undeservedly stigmatized aspect of human biology. It encourages trans representation by giving transfeminine characters access to a Merit on the basis of being feminine. It generates discussion of gender. And it does all of it in a way that is highly t